# SetFleetAssignment — tell the behavior tree which areas belong to OTHER
# fleet members right now, and where this robot should start looking.
#
# Called by the GUI fleet coordinator (docs/MULTI_ROBOT.md) every couple of
# seconds while coordinated mowing is enabled, and once with an empty list
# when it is switched off. Robots never call it on each other directly.
#
# Effects on the tree:
#   * GetNextUnmowedArea skips every index in excluded_areas, exactly as it
#     skips areas already completed or attempted this session. When nothing
#     but excluded areas remains the run ends as MOWING_COMPLETE and the
#     robot docks — the fleet's other members own the rest.
#   * A FollowStrip pass whose area becomes excluded mid-mow (two robots
#     picked the same area; the coordinator's tie-break told this one to
#     yield) saves its resume cursor, stops the blade and ends the pass; the
#     area is not charged to its no-progress budget.
#   * preferred_start_index rotates the ascending area scan so idle fleet
#     members do not all race for area 0: the scan starts there and wraps to
#     the lower indices afterwards. -1 keeps the plain ascending order. It is
#     ignored during a targeted run (~/start_in_area).
#
# The write is deferred to the BT tick thread like ~/clear_coverage_resume,
# so the request is acknowledged before it is applied.
uint32[] excluded_areas
int32 preferred_start_index
string reason
---
bool success
string message
